## Problem: Find the top 10 most popular routes with the average duration in minutes taken by customers and subscribers in New York 
## What I learned: the order of select will change the order of the columns, make sure you reference the columns in group by and not the aliases 

SELECT 
  usertype,
  COUNT(*) AS num_trips,
  CONCAT(start_station_name," to ", end_station_name) AS route,
  ROUND(AVG(tripduration/60), 2) AS avg_duration
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.citibike_trips`
GROUP BY 
  start_station_name, end_station_name, usertype 
ORDER BY 
  num_trips DESC
LIMIT 10 
